                <pb facs="0635" n="491" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg491"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10637: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Perkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-28T12:00:00+08:00">November 28,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received November 28—3:20 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1050. Department’s 388, November 26, 7 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>I am replying to the Minister for Foreign Affairs as indicated in the
                        Legation’s 1030, November 22, 10 p.m., third paragraph, but am incorporating
                        in the note the phraseology employed in paragraph 1 of the Department’s
                        telegram under reference.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>I am also telegraphing the text of the note to the commander in chief and
                        to the American Consul General at Canton and am informing the latter of the
                        content of paragraph 2 of the Department’s telegram.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
